  "title": "Blindfolds, dark glasses, closed eyes",
  "heading": "Close the eyes",
  "description": "Darkness in visual art: Blindfolds, dark glasses, closed eyes, blindness.",
  "source_encoding": "utf-8",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Close the eyes",
      "links": [],
      "level": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "But what must we do? Where lies the path? How come to behold the inaccessible Beauty, which seems to dwell in sacred precincts, apart from the common ways where even the profane can see?",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "He that has the strength, let him arise and withdraw into himself, foregoing all that is known by the eyes, turning away forever from the material beauty that once made his joy. When he perceives the graceful shapes displayed by material bodies, let him not pursue: he must know they are copies, vestiges, shadows, and must hasten away towards That which they tell of.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "[....]",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "What then is our course, what the manner of our flight? This is not a journey for the feet; the feet bring us only from land to land. Nor need you think of coach or ship to carry you away. All this order of things you must set aside and refuse to see. You must close the eyes and call instead upon another vision which is to be waked within you – a vision, the birth-right of all, which few turn to use.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Plotinus: The Six Enneads , 250 C.E.\n\nFirst Ennead, Sixth Tractate (on Beauty), Section 8.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Qu'as-tu vu dans ton exil?\n\nDisait à Spencer sa femme,\n\nA Rome, à Vienne, à Pergame,\n\nA Calcutta?",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Rien!... fit-il.\n\nVeux-tu découvrir le monde?\n\nFerme tes yeux, Rosemonde.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Jean Giraudoux: Suzanne et le Pacifique, Paris, 1921, p. 186",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Set to music by Arthur Honegger:\n\nPetit Cours de Morale, H. 148 no. 5, 1941.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Sluit uwe oogen op het licht:\n\ndieper zal het branden...\n\n\n\nKeer uw zinnen van den dag:\n\nlanger zal hij duren...",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Karel van de Woestijne: God aan zee.\n\nBussum, 1926, p. 58.",
      "links": []
    },
